1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:13,162
Every P2P crypto deal has a trust paradox: send Avalanche upfront and risk getting scammed; deliver your work first and risk getting ghosted; or use a centralized escrow and go back to trusting a middleman.

2
00:00:13,162 --> 00:00:26,062
Meet SafeDeal — non-custodial P2P escrow on Avalanche, where smart contracts hold the funds, RFC 8785 locks the terms, and no admin can ever touch your funds.

3
00:00:26,062 --> 00:00:28,150
Flow 1: Cooperative Trade.

4
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:30,175
The seller drafts deal terms.

5
00:00:30,175 --> 00:00:40,262
SafeDeal hashes them deterministically with RFC 8785 in both TypeScript and Rust, then anchors the terms hash on Avalanche Fuji.

6
00:00:40,262 --> 00:00:45,325
The buyer funds the vault, the seller marks delivery, and the buyer releases payment.

7
00:00:45,325 --> 00:00:56,062
Notice SafeDeal uses Pull-Payment withdraw — funds are credited to claimable balances rather than pushed inline, eliminating reentrancy and reverting-contract attacks.

8
00:00:56,062 --> 00:00:59,425
Flow 2: Open-Buyer and Refund Protection.

9
00:00:59,425 --> 00:01:00,975
Need a public payment link?

10
00:01:00,975 --> 00:01:06,187
Leave the buyer address blank — the first wallet to fund locks in as the buyer.

11
00:01:06,187 --> 00:01:17,175
And if a seller misses the delivery deadline, or issues a voluntary refund, the buyer reclaims 100% of their funds directly on-chain without asking anyone for permission.

12
00:01:17,175 --> 00:01:21,725
Flow 3: Dispute and 2-of-3 Consensus.

13
00:01:21,725 --> 00:01:32,687
When a deal goes wrong, participants upload private evidence validated by binary magic-bytes and gated by Sign-In with Ethereum — outsiders get a strict 403 error.

14
00:01:32,687 --> 00:01:42,575
Unlike traditional escrows where a single arbiter has god-mode, SafeDeal requires 2-of-3 matching votes across the buyer, the seller, and the arbiter.

15
00:01:42,575 --> 00:01:44,212
And if everyone ghosts?

16
00:01:44,212 --> 00:01:52,587
After 14 days, anyone can trigger a timeout resolution for a deterministic 50/50 split — zero trapped funds.

17
00:01:52,587 --> 00:02:02,200
Built with Solidity plus Foundry invariant fuzzing, a Clean Architecture Rust backend on Railway, and a reload-safe React UI live on Avalanche Fuji.

18
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,800
Try SafeDeal today at avalanche-9b099.web.app.

